# Button hierarchy

Apply these rules on every page (and when correcting existing pages).

## Variants

1. **One default (primary) button per page** — the main commit action (Save / Create / primary workflow CTA).
2. **All other section or footer secondary actions** use `variant="outline"`.
3. **Tertiary actions inside sections** use icon-only, link-style, or `variant="ghost"` (outline without border). Prefer Lucide glyphs over text when the action is clear.
4. **Destructive secondary actions** (Delete, Reject, Revoke): `variant="outline"` plus
   `class="text-destructive hover:bg-destructive/10 hover:text-destructive"` — not `variant="destructive"`.
5. **Exception — two defaults allowed** when a new primary action is offered while the usual primary is disabled (e.g. Reporting workflow awaiting approval: Approve may be default while Save is unavailable).

Dialogs/modals are a separate surface: one default CTA inside the dialog is OK.

## Footer placement

4. Main (default) button: **left**.
5. Secondary buttons: **right** (`justify-between` or equivalent).

## Header placement

6. All header actions sit on the **right**. Among them, **Back is always leftmost** (first in the flex order).

## Icons

7. Every button has a suitable Lucide glyph before the label. See `button-action-icons.mdc`.

## Do not

- Do not put Delete/Reject as filled `destructive` when they are secondary footer/header actions.
- Do not put Back after other header actions.
- Do not leave multiple unrelated default buttons on the same page body (dialogs excluded; exception #5 applies).
